reated in the 15th century [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texcotzingo]; The site had waterworks and terraces (hydraulic projects and terrace gardens) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texcotzingo]; The waterworks and terraces made previously un-arable land lush [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texcotzingo]; The lush gardens grew maize, beans and squash [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texcotzingo]"}]'::jsonb),
