lobroges [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cularo]; The inhabitants wished to thank the emperor Gratian for creating the bishopric and renamed the town Gratianopolis [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cularo]; The renaming to Gratianopolis took place in 381 [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Histoire_de_Grenoble]; The name Gratianopolis became Grenoble [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cularo]; Gallo-Roman walls remain in Grenoble [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cularo]"}]'::jsonb),
